Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the QAYEM Perfumes Next.js project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed Dependencies
- Added `@vercel/analytics@^2.0.1` package
- Added `@vercel/speed-insights@^2.0.0` package (was referenced but not installed)

### 2. Modified Files
- `src/app/layout.tsx`: Added Analytics component integration
  - Imported `Analytics` from `@vercel/analytics/next`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component to the root layout body, placed after `<SpeedInsights />`

### 3. Updated Lock Files
- `package-lock.json`: Updated with new dependencies

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart), the implementation uses the Next.js App Router approach:

1. The Analytics component is imported from `@vercel/analytics/next`
2. The component is placed in the root layout file (`src/app/layout.tsx`)
3. The component is positioned at the end of the `<body>` tag, following the existing SpeedInsights component pattern

## Framework Detection
- Framework: Next.js 16.2.10 with App Router (TypeScript)
- Package Manager: npm (detected from package-lock.json)

## Verification Steps Completed
✓ Build completed successfully with no errors
✓ TypeScript compilation passed
✓ All 26 pages rendered correctly
✓ Linter ran without introducing new errors (pre-existing warnings unrelated to this change)

## How It Works

Once deployed to Vercel, the Analytics component will:
- Automatically track page views
- Collect anonymous usage data
- Send analytics to your Vercel dashboard
- Require no additional configuration

## Next Steps for User

1. Deploy the application to Vercel using `vercel deploy`
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics section)
3. Visit your site to generate analytics data
4. Check the Network tab for requests to `/<unique-path>/view` to verify tracking is active
5. View analytics data in your Vercel dashboard

The implementation follows the existing code patterns in the project and integrates seamlessly with the already-installed SpeedInsights component.
